<%#
  T-26a — THE OWNED ISSUE REPORT WIDGET (FR-01).

  What used to be here resolved `IssueListReportTemplate.in_project_and_global(project)`
  — a base-plugin class that enforced NO visibility — and then rendered a partial that
  iframed the base plugin's own `report_content_report_template_path`. Both are gone. The
  lookup is `WidgetReport`, which starts from `Template.visible(actor)`, and the render is
  `Reporting::ReportRun`, which is the same producer the template editor's preview uses.

  THE QUERY IS NO LONGER REQUIRED. The old branch was `if query && report_template`, so a
  widget with a template and no saved query rendered its settings form for ever.
  `Reporting::ReportScope` answers "this project's visible issues" for a nil query id and
  the project's subtree for a real one, so the honest condition is the template alone.

  `user` rather than `User.current`, EVERYWHERE INCLUDING THE QUERY PICKER (INV-1). The
  helper passes the actor explicitly and `WidgetReport` requires one. `Query.visible` takes
  its actor as an optional first argument and falls back to `User.current` when none is
  given (`redmine/app/models/query.rb:385`), so the picker below used to read it ambiently
  — the same answer on this surface today, and exactly the silent drift the module header
  warns about for "a future scheduled or shared surface". Found by the independent review
  of T-26a and fixed rather than annotated.
%>
<%
  block ||= 'report_by_issues'
  settings ||= tab.block_settings(block)
  widget = RedmineReporterDashboards::WidgetReport.render(
    project: project, actor: user, block: block, settings: settings, logger: Rails.logger
  )
%>

<% if widget %>
  <%= render partial: 'reporter_project_pages/report',
             locals: { block: block, widget: widget, user: user,
                       project: project, tab: tab } %>
<% elsif editable %>
  <%= render partial: 'reporter_project_pages/report_settings',
             locals: { block: block, settings: settings, report_type: :issues,
                       queries: IssueQuery.visible(user).where(project_id: [nil, project.id]).sorted,
                       report_templates: RedmineReporterDashboards::WidgetReport.templates_for(
                         project: project, actor: user, source: 'issues'
                       ),
                       project: project, tab: tab } %>
<% else %>
  <p class="nodata"><%= l(:label_no_data) %></p>
<% end %>
